      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agent-tools): add request timeout to remote media fetches",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe agent media loading tools (`image_tool`, `image_generate`, `pdf_tool`) already pass `readIdleTimeoutMs` (idle timeout between data chunks) to `loadWebMedia`/`loadWebMediaRaw` but have no overall request timeout for remote HTTP fetches. A server that accepts the connection then hangs before sending any data will hold the download open indefinitely.\n\nThis is the same pattern Alix-007 is systematically fixing across channel extensions (telegram #103020, nodes-camera #103019, qqbot #103018).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe shared `loadWebMedia` / `loadWebMediaRaw` helpers now support `timeoutMs` in `WebMediaOptions` (#103206). The agent tool callers simply weren't passing it through.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPrevents indefinite hangs on remote media fetches in `image_tool`, `image_generate`, and `pdf_tool` when the remote server never responds.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `media-tool-shared.ts`: added `REMOTE_MEDIA_TIMEOUT_MS = 120_000` alongside existing `REMOTE_MEDIA_READ_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS`\n- `image-tool.ts`, `image-generate-tool.ts`, `pdf-tool.ts`: import and pass `timeoutMs: REMOTE_MEDIA_TIMEOUT_MS` conditionally with `...(isHttpUrl ? {...} : {})`\n\nChange: 24 insertions, 3 deletions across 4 files.\n",
        "branch": "fix/agent-tools-media-fetch-timeout",
